			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@vsaw\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>vsaw</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> man I hadn’t read the page, just heard about it, and I wonder why they believe they need that resolution in time and bits (especially in time, 20k seems silly). I’m hardly a domain expert but the sEEG and ECog data colleagues I worked with used was sampled at like, 1 to 2k roundabout, and that was good enough for speech processes</p><p>(I was also going to say “and why not lossy compress optimized for downstream tasks” but I guess optimizing such compression would be pretty complicated)</p>",
